         $WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"THE TEMPLE OF HERMES' Features"$$FG$

$FG,5$Hermes co-use features (new in this fork):$FG$
* Hermes agent daemon on COM1 at 115200 8n1: HBEACON / HREQ / HRPL / HEVT frames; ping, eval HolyC, list tasks and windows, focus, mouse, text, mode, clipboard, files, events, idle.
* Exact DolDoc plain-text export of the focused window or all visible windows, with cursor and window geometry.  Ground truth, not glyph OCR.
* Presence banner (user|shared|agent) and a distinct agent crosshair, separate from the human pointer.
* Event stream: ready, task_spawned, window_opened, prompt_waiting, compile_error, mode_changed, danger_blocked.
* Boots straight to a USER session; the live CD does not stop at the install or tour prompts.  OSInstall is still available from USER mode.
* Agent-aware input guards: in AGENT mode, YorN, AreYouSure, Fmt, OSInstall, and BootHDIns refuse and emit danger_blocked.  SHARED still refuses format and install.
* Temple of Hermes branding, Start page, boot banner, debugger banner, and 16-colour art set in Hermes/Art.

$FG,5$Inherited from TinkerOS (upstream):$FG$
* $FG,4$$TX,"USB bootable image",HTML="https://github.com/tinkeros/TinkerOS/releases"$$FG$ with live RAM boot and install support.
* Extra apps (After Egypt, Castle Frankenstein 2, Oregon Trail, Sudoku, Wordle).
* Improved installer with resolution options and TOS supplemental discs.
* Repaste last command with $FG,2$<F8>$FG$; toggle blinking/scrolling with $FG,2$<SHIFT-F8>$FG$.
* Screenshot with $FG,2$<F9>$FG$; screen clip with $FG,2$<SHIFT-F9>$FG$.
* ATA/IDE/Legacy or AHCI installation, VMMouse, OPL sound, extra colours, and higher resolutions.
* Backwards compatibility with TempleOS except programs that use VGA registers directly or hijack the graphics system.

$FG,5$Upstream:$FG$
* TempleOS features: $FG,4$$TX,"TempleOS",HTML="https://tinkeros.github.io/WbTempleOS/Doc/Features.html"$$FG$
* TinkerOS features: $LK,"TinkerOS feature list",A="FI:::/Doc/TinkerOS.DD"$
* About and credits: $LK,"About THE TEMPLE OF HERMES",A="FI:::/Doc/AboutHermes.DD"$

